issues remain open; this PR implements their corrective composition without claiming the original live matrix or performance targets complete.\n\n## Workflow evidence\n\nWorkflow-status comment: https://github.com/smota/agentflow-sdlc/issues/301#issuecomment-5865551409\nHandover comments: exception: one consolidated workflow-status comment plus explicit scoped helper contracts; same-platform helpers are disclosed below.\nRole-pass summary: analyst/planner preserved A1-A9; developer implemented scoped corrections; tester ran regressions and actual CLI/source probes; reviewer returned privacy, path-scope and recovery races to implementation; final evidence synthesis retains external qualification limits.\nValidation evidence: docs/maintainers/process-autonomy-completion.md and CI on this candidate. Local scratch logs are not durable approval records.\n\n## Agent review\n\n- Implemented by: codex\n- Launcher: codex\n- Executor: codex-cli\n- Transport: local-cli\n- Delegation boundary: current-session\n- Model / runtime: Codex desktop parent; gpt-6-sol implementation helpers, gpt-6-luna bounded docs/review; separate native gpt-5.6-luna CLI probe\n- Review: self-review\n- Workflow profile: standard\n- Merge owner: human/operator\n- Mode: multi-agent\n- Self-review disclosure: Codex authored and reviewed the changes with separate read-only helpers. Grok supplied independent architecture advice, not final code or human acceptance. No human-review attestation is claimed.\n- Regression test: added\n\nThe user authorized autonomous completion and experimental merge. That delegation does not modify generic high-assurance policy. Live Codex write qualification remains blocked by this host's effective read-only sandbox; the installed Meshloop binary lacks required integration capabilities. New edit dispatch defaults to refusal without qualified capability and explicit source-evidence disclosure.\n\n## Role attribution matrix\n\n| Phase | Role | Planned owner | Actual platform | 